\strong{Reading a \code{hidden_column} finding as a gutter column.} It is not
one. The detector requires empty \strong{and} narrower than 0.1 inch,
precisely so the deliberate half-inch gutter columns in the house
JTCVS templates do not trip it. A finding here is a real spacer.

\strong{Treating \code{embedded_footnote} or \code{markup} as proof.} They are the two
heuristic detectors of the six. \code{embedded_footnote} matches a marker
character opening a cell in a table's last row, and a legitimate last
row that happens to start that way matches it too. \code{markup} matches a
pair of \code{^} or \code{~} characters, and a URL with two tildes matches it.
Read either as a prompt to look, not a verdict.

\strong{Expecting a repair.} This is read-only and never modifies the
file. Fix what it reports in Word, or rebuild the table through
\code{\link[=hv_man_table_save]{hv_man_table_save()}}.
